WEBVTT

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.323
Did you know our

00:00:01.343 --> 00:00:03.230
SALARY CYCLE is changing?

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.339
Here's what it means for you.

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.647
Up to now, it has followed

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.860
a JANUARY-to-DECEMBER cycle

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.851
12 months, one cycle.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.282
MERIT

00:00:14.302 --> 00:00:18.250
Projected market salary movement

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.141
BONUS

00:00:19.161 --> 00:00:22.880
Estimated Company Performance KPIs

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.754
HSE  ·  FINANCE  ·  PERFORMANCE

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.510
Now, we're moving to a new cycle.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.944
From APRIL to MARCH

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.402
Merit increases and promotions

00:00:36.422 --> 00:00:38.460
take effect on APRIL 1

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.591
That's where the cycle now begins.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:43.143
BONUS

00:00:43.163 --> 00:00:46.050
paid in the MARCH payroll

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.880
MARCH is the last month

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.274
of the cycle

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.570
One thing that isn't changing

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.232
Your PERFORMANCE APPRAISAL

00:00:54.252 --> 00:00:55.960
stays on the same schedule

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.402
and it will still close

00:00:57.422 --> 00:00:58.722
in DECEMBER

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.040
One more thing worth knowing

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.360
Say your merit increase is 5%

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.968
The implementation year covers

00:01:08.988 --> 00:01:12.050
15 MONTHS instead of 12

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.604
5% ÷ 12 = about 0.417%

00:01:15.624 --> 00:01:17.270
per month

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:20.170
Multiply that by 15 months

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.787
and the equivalent becomes

00:01:22.807 --> 00:01:24.107
6.25%

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.940
APRIL to MARCH

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.049
That's the one to remember.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.350
Why the change?

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.540
Closer to market best practice

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.638
More relevant information

00:01:36.658 --> 00:01:38.739
when we set salaries

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.010
If you have questions,

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:43.723
HR is ready to help.
